From: Ross Cawston <ross@r-sc.ca>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pse-pd: make room for a PI without recursing

With the static budget strategy, making room for a PI whose request
doesn't fit can recurse until the stack overflows. The PI turns off the
PIs of lower priority in its power domain, a whole priority level at a
time, with pse_disable_pi_pol(), which then retries the power delivery
of the PIs waiting for power in the domain. The PI is waiting for power
itself when its PD is classified, and during every retry of the domain:
after a disconnection, an admin disable or a priority change. The retry
then powers the PI just turned off again with the budget it freed, if it
comes first in the domain, and allocates the budget of the PI again,
from inside its own allocation, which turns the other PI off again, and
so on. If the PI turned off comes after it, the retry powers the PI
itself, from inside its own allocation, which can then allocate it a
second time. On an admin enable, where the PI isn't waiting yet, the PI
turned off is powered again right away, and the priorities never take
effect.

Make room without retrying the power domain:

- Select the PIs to turn off before turning any off: only the enabled
  PIs of lower priority that hold budget, from the lowest priority and,
  at the same priority, from the last one, until their budget and the
  unclaimed budget make room; then leave out those that aren't needed,
  from the highest priority. If that can't make room, nothing is turned
  off. Budget that such a PI holds while it is off is freed, as it is
  not in use.
- Turn them off and request the budget. If that fails, or enabling the
  PI fails and it can be disabled again, give each PI turned off the
  budget it held back and enable it again, without making room for it
  in turn.
- Notify the PIs that stay off as over budget, once that is known.
- After an admin enable or a classification that made room, retry the
  power domain for the budget left over.

Retry the PIs of a power domain from the highest priority, as
ethtool-netlink.rst documents for the power-up order, so that a PI of
lower priority doesn't take the budget that one of higher priority
waits for, only to be turned off for it again. Events reported
together are still handled one PI at a time, in the order of their
index. This drops on purpose the cut-off that prio_max was meant for,
and which never took effect, as it was reset for every PI: a PI of
lower priority can still take budget that a PI of higher priority can't
use, as that one can turn it off later.

As before, only the PIs of the PSE controller of the PI are turned off
and retried, also when its power domain is shared with another
controller. Only the unclaimed budget of the domain's own supply is
counted: when a supply it is supplied from is short of budget, the
request fails after the PIs are turned off, they get their budget back,
and the priorities don't apply to that shortage.

Sashiko, the netdev AI review bot, pointed out in its review of v1 of
"net: pse-pd: don't enable a PI again while disabling it" (the Link
below) that leaving out the retry alone leaves PIs off for nothing. Not
reproduced on hardware; build-tested only.

Fixes: ffef61d6d273 ("net: pse-pd: Add support for budget evaluation strategies")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/179243532177.3135.6604862508015344848@kernel.org/
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/pse-pd/pse_core.c b/drivers/net/pse-pd/pse_core.c
index 0a58466..4ed6ee6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pse-pd/pse_core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pse-pd/pse_core.c
@@ -424,7 +424,7 @@ pse_pi_is_admin_enable_pending(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id)
 }
 
 static int _pse_pi_delivery_power_sw_pw_ctrl(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
-					     int id,
+					     int id, bool *made_room,
 					     struct netlink_ext_ack *extack);
 
 /**
@@ -433,36 +433,36 @@ static int _pse_pi_delivery_power_sw_pw_ctrl(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
  * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE controller device
  * @pw_d: a pointer to the PSE power domain
  *
- * Scans all ports in the specified power domain and attempts to enable power
- * delivery to any ports that have admin enable state set but don't yet have
- * hardware power enabled. Used when there are changes in connection status,
- * admin state, or priority that might allow previously unpowered ports to
- * receive power, especially in over-budget conditions.
+ * Scans all ports in the specified power domain, from the highest priority
+ * (lowest value) to the lowest, and attempts to enable power delivery to any
+ * ports that have admin enable state set but don't yet have hardware power
+ * enabled. Used when there are changes in connection status, admin state, or
+ * priority that might allow previously unpowered ports to receive power,
+ * especially in over-budget conditions. Going from the highest priority keeps
+ * a port of lower priority from taking the budget that one of higher priority
+ * waits for, only to be turned off for it again. A port of lower priority can
+ * still take budget that one of higher priority can't use: the port of higher
+ * priority can turn it off later.
  */
 static void pse_pw_d_retry_power_delivery(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
 					  struct pse_power_domain *pw_d)
 {
-	int i, ret = 0;
+	int prio, i;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
-		int prio_max = pcdev->nr_lines;
-		struct netlink_ext_ack extack;
-
-		if (pcdev->pi[i].pw_d != pw_d)
-			continue;
+	for (prio = 0; prio < pcdev->nr_lines; prio++) {
+		for (i = 0; i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
+			struct netlink_ext_ack extack;
 
-		if (!pse_pi_is_admin_enable_pending(pcdev, i))
-			continue;
+			if (pcdev->pi[i].pw_d != pw_d ||
+			    pcdev->pi[i].prio != prio)
+				continue;
 
-		/* Do not try to enable PI with a lower prio (higher value)
-		 * than one which already can't be enabled.
-		 */
-		if (pcdev->pi[i].prio > prio_max)
-			continue;
+			if (!pse_pi_is_admin_enable_pending(pcdev, i))
+				continue;
 
-		ret = _pse_pi_delivery_power_sw_pw_ctrl(pcdev, i, &extack);
-		if (ret == -ERANGE)
-			prio_max = pcdev->pi[i].prio;
+			_pse_pi_delivery_power_sw_pw_ctrl(pcdev, i, NULL,
+							  &extack);
+		}
 	}
 }
 
@@ -562,63 +562,265 @@ static int _pse_pi_disable(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id)
 }
 
 /**
- * pse_disable_pi_pol - Disable a PI on a power budget policy
+ * pse_pi_notify - Notify PSE events of a PI
+ * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
+ * @id: index of the PSE PI
+ * @notifs: PSE events
+ */
+static void pse_pi_notify(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
+			  unsigned long notifs)
+{
+	struct pse_ntf ntf = {
+		.id = id,
+		.notifs = notifs,
+	};
+
+	kfifo_in_spinlocked(&pcdev->ntf_fifo, &ntf, 1, &pcdev->ntf_fifo_lock);
+	schedule_work(&pcdev->ntf_work);
+}
+
+/**
+ * pse_pis_lowest_prio - Find the PI with the lowest priority in a set of PIs
+ * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
+ * @pis: bitmap of PIs
+ *
+ * Return: the index of the PI with the lowest priority (highest value), the
+ *	   last one of them at the same priority, or -1 if @pis is empty
+ */
+static int pse_pis_lowest_prio(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
+			       const unsigned long *pis)
+{
+	int i, id = -1;
+
+	for_each_set_bit(i, pis, pcdev->nr_lines) {
+		if (id < 0 || pcdev->pi[i].prio >= pcdev->pi[id].prio)
+			id = i;
+	}
+
+	return id;
+}
+
+/**
+ * pse_pis_highest_prio - Find the PI with the highest priority in a set of PIs
+ * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
+ * @pis: bitmap of PIs
+ *
+ * Return: the index of the PI with the highest priority (lowest value), the
+ *	   first one of them at the same priority, or -1 if @pis is empty
+ */
+static int pse_pis_highest_prio(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
+				const unsigned long *pis)
+{
+	int i, id = -1;
+
+	for_each_set_bit(i, pis, pcdev->nr_lines) {
+		if (id < 0 || pcdev->pi[i].prio < pcdev->pi[id].prio)
+			id = i;
+	}
+
+	return id;
+}
+
+/**
+ * pse_pw_d_select_pis_to_disable - Select the PIs to disable to make room for
+ *				    the power request of a PI
+ * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
+ * @id: index of the PSE PI that requests power
+ * @pw_req: power requested in mW
+ * @off_pw: array of nr_lines power budgets in mW, all 0 on entry; set to the
+ *	    budget of each PI selected
+ *
+ * Only the enabled PIs of this PSE controller that hold budget in the power
+ * domain of the PI, with a lower priority (higher value), are selected. The
+ * budget that such a PI holds while it is off is freed, as it is not in use.
+ * The PIs are picked from the lowest priority, and at the same priority from
+ * the last one, until their budget and the unclaimed budget make room for the
+ * request. Then the picks that are not needed are left out, from the highest
+ * priority, so that each PI selected is needed.
+ *
+ * Only the unclaimed budget of the domain's own supply is counted. When a
+ * supply it is supplied from is short of budget, the request fails after the
+ * PIs selected are disabled, and they get their budget back: the priorities
+ * don't apply to that shortage.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success, -ERANGE if disabling all those PIs can't make room,
+ *	   with @off_pw all 0 again, and another failure value on error
+ */
+static int pse_pw_d_select_pis_to_disable(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
+					  int id, int pw_req, int *off_pw)
+{
+	struct pse_pi *pi = &pcdev->pi[id];
+	unsigned long *pis;
+	int i, ret = 0;
+	s64 pw;
+
+	pis = bitmap_zalloc(pcdev->nr_lines, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!pis)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
+		if (pcdev->pi[i].pw_d != pi->pw_d ||
+		    pcdev->pi[i].prio <= pi->prio ||
+		    !pcdev->pi[i].pw_allocated_mW)
+			continue;
+
+		ret = pse_pi_is_hw_enabled(pcdev, i);
+		if (ret > 0)
+			__set_bit(i, pis);
+		else if (!ret)
+			pse_pi_deallocate_pw_budget(&pcdev->pi[i]);
+	}
+	ret = 0;
+
+	pw = regulator_get_unclaimed_power_budget(pi->pw_d->supply);
+	while (pw < pw_req) {
+		i = pse_pis_lowest_prio(pcdev, pis);
+		if (i < 0) {
+			memset(off_pw, 0, pcdev->nr_lines * sizeof(*off_pw));
+			ret = -ERANGE;
+			goto out;
+		}
+
+		__clear_bit(i, pis);
+		off_pw[i] = pcdev->pi[i].pw_allocated_mW;
+		pw += off_pw[i];
+	}
+
+	bitmap_zero(pis, pcdev->nr_lines);
+	for (i = 0; i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
+		if (off_pw[i])
+			__set_bit(i, pis);
+	}
+
+	while ((i = pse_pis_highest_prio(pcdev, pis)) >= 0) {
+		__clear_bit(i, pis);
+		if (pw - off_pw[i] >= pw_req) {
+			pw -= off_pw[i];
+			off_pw[i] = 0;
+		}
+	}
+
+out:
+	bitmap_free(pis);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/**
+ * pse_pi_power_again - Give a PI disabled to make room its budget back, and
+ *			enable it
  * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
+ * @pw_d: a pointer to the PSE power domain
  * @id: index of the PSE PI
+ * @pw: power budget in mW that the PI held
  *
  * Return: 0 on success and failure value on error
  */
-static int pse_disable_pi_pol(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id)
+static int pse_pi_power_again(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
+			      struct pse_power_domain *pw_d, int id, int pw)
 {
-	unsigned long notifs = ETHTOOL_PSE_EVENT_OVER_BUDGET;
-	struct pse_ntf ntf = {};
 	int ret;
 
-	dev_dbg(pcdev->dev, "Disabling PI %d to free power budget\n", id);
-
-	ret = _pse_pi_disable(pcdev, id);
+	ret = regulator_request_power_budget(pw_d->supply, pw);
 	if (ret)
-		notifs |= ETHTOOL_PSE_EVENT_SW_PW_CONTROL_ERROR;
-	else if (pse_pw_d_is_sw_pw_control(pcdev, pcdev->pi[id].pw_d))
-		pse_pw_d_retry_power_delivery(pcdev, pcdev->pi[id].pw_d);
+		return ret;
 
-	ntf.notifs = notifs;
-	ntf.id = id;
-	kfifo_in_spinlocked(&pcdev->ntf_fifo, &ntf, 1, &pcdev->ntf_fifo_lock);
-	schedule_work(&pcdev->ntf_work);
+	pcdev->pi[id].pw_allocated_mW = pw;
+	ret = pcdev->ops->pi_enable(pcdev, id);
+	/* Disabled again, or left with its budget if that fails too */
+	if (ret)
+		_pse_pi_disable(pcdev, id);
 
 	return ret;
 }
 
 /**
- * pse_disable_pi_prio - Disable all PIs of a given priority inside a PSE
- *			 power domain
+ * pse_pis_power_again - Power the PIs disabled to make room again
  * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
  * @pw_d: a pointer to the PSE power domain
- * @prio: priority
+ * @off_pw: array of nr_lines power budgets in mW, the budget that each PI
+ *	    disabled held and 0 for the others; all 0 on return
  *
- * Return: 0 on success and failure value on error
+ * From the highest priority, each PI gets back the budget it held, if it is
+ * still unclaimed, and is enabled again. A PI that can't stays disabled,
+ * waiting for power, and is notified as over budget when its budget is gone,
+ * or of the error when it fails to enable.
+ */
+static void pse_pis_power_again(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
+				struct pse_power_domain *pw_d, int *off_pw)
+{
+	unsigned long notifs;
+	int prio, i, ret;
+
+	for (prio = 0; prio < pcdev->nr_lines; prio++) {
+		for (i = 0; i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
+			if (!off_pw[i] || pcdev->pi[i].prio != prio)
+				continue;
+
+			ret = pse_pi_power_again(pcdev, pw_d, i, off_pw[i]);
+			if (ret) {
+				notifs = ret == -ERANGE ?
+					 ETHTOOL_PSE_EVENT_OVER_BUDGET :
+					 ETHTOOL_PSE_EVENT_SW_PW_CONTROL_ERROR;
+				pse_pi_notify(pcdev, i, notifs);
+			}
+
+			off_pw[i] = 0;
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+/**
+ * pse_pi_make_room - Disable PIs of lower priority to make room for the power
+ *		      request of a PI, and request it
+ * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
+ * @id: index of the PSE PI that requests power
+ * @pw_req: power requested in mW
+ * @off_pw: array of nr_lines power budgets in mW, all 0 on entry; set to the
+ *	    budget that each PI disabled held, and all 0 again on failure
+ *
+ * On failure, each PI disabled gets its budget back and is enabled again if it
+ * can. A PI that fails to disable is left as it is, with its budget.
+ *
+ * Return: 0 on success, -ERANGE if disabling PIs of lower priority can't make
+ *	   room, and another failure value on error
  */
-static int pse_disable_pi_prio(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
-			       struct pse_power_domain *pw_d,
-			       int prio)
+static int pse_pi_make_room(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
+			    int pw_req, int *off_pw)
 {
-	int i;
+	struct pse_power_domain *pw_d = pcdev->pi[id].pw_d;
+	int ret, i;
+
+	ret = pse_pw_d_select_pis_to_disable(pcdev, id, pw_req, off_pw);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
-		int ret;
+		if (!off_pw[i])
+			continue;
 
-		if (pcdev->pi[i].prio != prio ||
-		    pcdev->pi[i].pw_d != pw_d ||
-		    pse_pi_is_hw_enabled(pcdev, i) <= 0)
+		/* Not reached after a failure: still enabled */
+		if (ret) {
+			off_pw[i] = 0;
 			continue;
+		}
 
-		ret = pse_disable_pi_pol(pcdev, i);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+		dev_dbg(pcdev->dev, "Disabling PI %d to free power budget\n",
+			i);
+		ret = _pse_pi_disable(pcdev, i);
+		if (ret) {
+			/* Left alone, with its budget: its state is unknown */
+			off_pw[i] = 0;
+			pse_pi_notify(pcdev, i,
+				      ETHTOOL_PSE_EVENT_SW_PW_CONTROL_ERROR);
+		}
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regulator_request_power_budget(pw_d->supply, pw_req);
+	if (ret)
+		pse_pis_power_again(pcdev, pw_d, off_pw);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 /**
@@ -628,36 +830,41 @@ static int pse_disable_pi_prio(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
  * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
  * @id: index of the PSE control
  * @pw_req: power requested in mW
+ * @off_pw: NULL on entry, and left NULL unless the request doesn't fit; then
+ *	    set to an array of nr_lines power budgets in mW, the budget that
+ *	    each PI disabled to make room held, for the caller to free
  * @extack: extack for error reporting
  *
  * Allocates power using static budget evaluation strategy, where allocation
  * is based on PD classification. When insufficient budget is available,
- * lower-priority ports (higher priority numbers) are turned off first.
+ * lower-priority ports (higher priority numbers) are turned off, the lowest
+ * priority first, but only those needed, and only if that makes room.
  *
  * Return: 0 on success and failure value on error
  */
 static int
 pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget_static_prio(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
-				      int pw_req, struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
+				      int pw_req, int **off_pw,
+				      struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
 {
 	struct pse_pi *pi = &pcdev->pi[id];
-	int ret, _prio;
-
-	_prio = pcdev->nr_lines;
-	while (regulator_request_power_budget(pi->pw_d->supply, pw_req) == -ERANGE) {
-		if (_prio <= pi->prio) {
-			NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT(extack,
-					   "PI %d: not enough power budget available",
-					   id);
-			return -ERANGE;
-		}
+	int ret;
 
-		ret = pse_disable_pi_prio(pcdev, pi->pw_d, _prio);
-		if (ret < 0)
-			return ret;
+	ret = regulator_request_power_budget(pi->pw_d->supply, pw_req);
+	if (ret == -ERANGE) {
+		*off_pw = kcalloc(pcdev->nr_lines, sizeof(**off_pw),
+				  GFP_KERNEL);
+		if (!*off_pw)
+			return -ENOMEM;
 
-		_prio--;
+		ret = pse_pi_make_room(pcdev, id, pw_req, *off_pw);
 	}
+	if (ret == -ERANGE)
+		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT(extack,
+				   "PI %d: not enough power budget available",
+				   id);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	pi->pw_allocated_mW = pw_req;
 	return 0;
@@ -668,12 +875,16 @@ pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget_static_prio(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
  * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
  * @id: index of the PSE control
  * @pw_req: power requested in mW
+ * @off_pw: NULL on entry, and left NULL unless the static strategy had to make
+ *	    room; then set to an array of the budget that each PI disabled to
+ *	    make room held, for the caller to free
  * @extack: extack for error reporting
  *
  * Return: 0 on success and failure value on error
  */
 static int pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
-				     int pw_req, struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
+				     int pw_req, int **off_pw,
+				     struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
 {
 	struct pse_pi *pi = &pcdev->pi[id];
 
@@ -683,7 +894,7 @@ static int pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
 	/* PSE_BUDGET_EVAL_STRAT_STATIC */
 	if (pi->pw_d->budget_eval_strategy == PSE_BUDGET_EVAL_STRAT_STATIC)
 		return pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget_static_prio(pcdev, id, pw_req,
-							     extack);
+							     off_pw, extack);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -694,17 +905,24 @@ static int pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev, int id,
  *				       acquired.
  * @pcdev: a pointer to the PSE
  * @id: index of the PSE control
+ * @made_room: if not NULL, set to whether the PI got power and PIs of lower
+ *	       priority stay disabled for it, which can leave budget for PIs
+ *	       waiting for power
  * @extack: extack for error reporting
  *
  * Return: 0 on success and failure value on error
  */
 static int _pse_pi_delivery_power_sw_pw_ctrl(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
-					     int id,
+					     int id, bool *made_room,
 					     struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
 {
 	const struct pse_controller_ops *ops = pcdev->ops;
 	struct pse_pi *pi = &pcdev->pi[id];
-	int ret, pw_req;
+	int ret, pw_req, i;
+	int *off_pw = NULL;
+
+	if (made_room)
+		*made_room = false;
 
 	if (!ops->pi_get_pw_req) {
 		/* No power allocation management */
@@ -746,20 +964,36 @@ static int _pse_pi_delivery_power_sw_pw_ctrl(struct pse_controller_dev *pcdev,
 			pw_req = ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget(pcdev, id, pw_req, extack);
+	ret = pse_pi_allocate_pw_budget(pcdev, id, pw_req, &off_pw, extack);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto out;
 
 	ret = ops->pi_enable(pcdev, id);
 	if (ret) {
-		pse_pi_deallocate_pw_budget(pi);
 		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT(extack,
 				   "PI %d: enable error %d",
 				   id, ret);
-		return ret;
+		/* Disabled again, which frees its budget, the PIs disabled for
+		 * it get their power back. If that fails too, its state is
+		 * unknown: it keeps its budget, and they stay off.
+		 */
+		if (!_pse_pi_disable(pcdev, id) && off_pw)
+			pse_pis_power_again(pcdev, pi->pw_d, off_pw);
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	/* The PIs disabled to make room that stay off are over budget */
+	for (i = 0; off_pw && i < pcdev->nr_lines; i++) {
+		if (!off_pw[i])
+			continue;
+
+		pse_pi_notify(pcdev, i, ETHTOOL_PSE_EVENT_OVER_BUDGET);
+		if (made_room && !ret)
+			*made_room = true;
+	}
+
+out:
+	kfree(off_pw);
+	return ret;
